WEBVTT

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:23.620
Can you see?

00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:30.550
That star there is called Mars, 
and it's right next door to the Earth.

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:35.050
I heard that a lot of people are going 
to move there in the near future.

00:00:36.310 --> 00:00:38.300
I wonder what it's like.

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.000
Well, I guess it doesn't look so bad.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:46.470
If anything, it'd be better 
than this dead-end town.

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:51.240
I want to go...

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:01.330
Go! Do it!

00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:31.750
Hey, we should at least say goodbye...

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:36.970
The ones who burned down the 
mansion over an argument

00:01:36.970 --> 00:01:38.990
about pay are our parents.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:41.730
Now Sheila doesn't have anything, either.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:45.000
So it does all come down

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:47.020
to money...

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:26.790
Every inch of my body hurts.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:28.820
I broke my collarbone.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:30.690
Damn...

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:33.310
Isn't there some place that

00:02:33.310 --> 00:02:36.710
doesn't have gangs, 
discrimination, or poverty?

00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:39.470
Seriously. Something better than here...

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.860
Please! Please!

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:01.610
We have nowhere else to go! Please!

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:08.140
Hey, what's going on?

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.900
Oh, Captain Komachi.

00:03:09.900 --> 00:03:12.440
These guys popped out of nowhere 
and asked to join the crew.

00:03:13.120 --> 00:03:14.520
Volunteers?

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:15.670
Um...

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:19.150
Where's the next place for the interviews?

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:24.610
Sheila's here!

00:03:24.610 --> 00:03:27.130
Is it really her? Does she have a heartbeat?

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:28.720
Hey! Don't touch my chest!

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:29.740
Hey!

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:32.390
<i>She always accepted us 
without any hesitation.</i>

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:36.450
<i>If we were reborn, 
I wanted to live like this.</i>

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:40.690
<i>Sheila's the one...</i>

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:45.250
<i>...I admired.</i>

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:26.820
<i>The huntsman spider feeds 
mainly on cockroaches,</i>

00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:30.310
<i>and has spread almost 
as fast as the cockroach.</i>

00:05:31.620 --> 00:05:34.700
<i>Its body hair detects even 
the most subtle movement of the air,</i>

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.770
<i>which allows it to read 
its prey's movements.</i>

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:42.830
<i>Then it stabs its prey, rips it apart,</i>

00:05:45.750 --> 00:05:46.980
<i>and eats it.</i>

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:53.450
<i>Even if other cockroaches come 
towards it when it's feeding,</i>

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:57.620
<i>it's ferocious enough to attack instantly.</i>

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:01.550
<i>I wanted you to be happier 
than anyone else.</i>

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:09.080
<i>Does losing money mean that your 
wishes get stolen away, too?!</i>

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:20.740
<i>However, the huntsman spider usually 
hunts by waiting in the shadows,</i>

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:23.160
<i>and its stamina isn't exactly high.</i>

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:33.530
Captain...

00:06:34.430 --> 00:06:35.470
Everyone...

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:37.720
I...

00:06:39.320 --> 00:06:41.610
Considering the fact that they might

00:06:41.610 --> 00:06:43.970
possess the virus we can't cultivate,

00:06:44.490 --> 00:06:46.520
we want to get as many samples as possible.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:52.570
Marcos!

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:56.640
We're going to beat the crap out 
of a heap of these roaches here.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.400
If some of them are still 
breathing, we'll capture them.

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:00.840
Yes, sir!

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:15.700
Don't run away, you roachy bastards.

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:52.490
The captain of the Bugs 2, 
Donatello K. Davis...

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:56.030
The powers he gained from his BUGS surgery...

00:07:56.030 --> 00:08:02.500
the ant that can lift a hundred 
times its own weight, the paraponera.

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:07.260
There should have been no way 
that it'd be passed on...

00:08:07.890 --> 00:08:12.510
All of the scientists back in the day 
said it was just God playing tricks.

00:08:13.210 --> 00:08:17.010
However, the God on Earth 
does not play tricks.

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:20.560
Their will and powers were passed down.

00:08:21.310 --> 00:08:23.770
Who are you talking about?

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:30.280
The leader of the Japanese and American 
No. 2 division, Michelle K. Davis.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:32.660
The Captain's...

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:36.780
She has two powers.

00:08:36.780 --> 00:08:40.540
First, what she inherited from her father.

00:08:42.210 --> 00:08:47.540
<i>One, two, three, four...</i>

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:54.640
Yes, the muscular strength 
of the paraponera...

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:09.780
And then the second power she gained 
from the Mosaic Organ Operation.

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:14.320
The base, once again, is insect-based.

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:24.230
<i>What kind of bug... is that?</i>

00:09:25.470 --> 00:09:26.900
<i>In the 20th century,</i>

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:31.440
<i>a peculiar action from a peculiar 
ant in Malaysia was observed.</i>

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:37.340
<i>The ant self-destructed.</i>

00:10:06.410 --> 00:10:08.330
These guys sure die easily.

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:12.340
<i>Nicknamed the blast ant,
it is a rare breed.</i>

00:10:14.870 --> 00:10:17.050
The powers can be passed down.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:20.260
We have confirmed that while 
observing another young man

00:10:20.260 --> 00:10:23.220
who underwent the surgery and training.

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:29.720
They will be our greatest weapons, 
as well as become our hope.

00:10:32.530 --> 00:10:36.490
Michelle K. Davis and Hizamaru Akari.

00:10:37.680 --> 00:10:39.550
Is Hizamaru Akari there now?

00:10:40.100 --> 00:10:41.800
On Mars?

00:10:41.800 --> 00:10:43.490
Do you know something?

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:49.260
First, I'll tell you our reasons.

00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:54.010
More than anything, 
we needed firepower on Mars.

00:10:54.010 --> 00:10:58.230
We needed as many highly 
ranked Japanese as we could get.

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:01.340
If something were to occur on Mars...

00:11:03.540 --> 00:11:06.640
Alex, keep an eye on the sky 
above the escape vessel.

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:08.640
Yeah, got it.

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:13.240
Leave those three to me.

00:11:29.570 --> 00:11:30.760
<i>It's strange...</i>

00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:37.300
<i>Whenever I mutate naturally, 
rage and fear make me lose my mind,</i>

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:41.070
<i>and it feels like the part of me 
that's not human takes over...</i>

00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:43.770
<i>But when I use the medicine...</i>

00:11:59.620 --> 00:12:02.280
<i>I feel like a pupa that's 
about to take flight,</i>

00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:05.340
<i>and I can see the world around me clearly.</i>

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:06.950
<i>I'm not scared!</i>

00:12:16.560 --> 00:12:19.750
That was for all of my friends 
who died on the ship.

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:25.470
And then...

00:12:28.550 --> 00:12:31.980
This is for pissing off Michelle-san

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:35.090
with that shitty breath of yours.

00:12:36.620 --> 00:12:38.530
But I'm not going to kill you.

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:40.710
And there's a reason for that...

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:46.900
Mars, huh?

00:13:13.780 --> 00:13:15.050
You're going to catch a cold.

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:19.840
Hey, can I see that doll?

00:13:19.840 --> 00:13:21.600
Huh? Sure...

00:13:22.730 --> 00:13:25.270
How sad. It's all broken.

00:13:25.730 --> 00:13:27.910
What are you doing here?

00:13:27.910 --> 00:13:29.880
I live in that hospital.

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:32.450
My name is Sakurato

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:35.820
Harukaze Sakurato. I'm ten years old.

00:13:36.320 --> 00:13:38.460
I'm Hizamaru Akari...

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.210
I'm twenty.

00:13:40.210 --> 00:13:43.690
Huh... That's a pretty 
cool name, Hizamaru-san.

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:47.060
Harukaze...

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:53.640
By the way, why are you in the hospital?

00:13:57.350 --> 00:14:03.270
My illness is too hard for the doctors 
in Japan to treat, so I moved.

00:14:09.200 --> 00:14:10.410
Hizamaru-san?

00:14:11.810 --> 00:14:14.500
Sorry... I've got to get going.

00:14:16.510 --> 00:14:17.740
Eh? Hey, what about this?

00:14:17.740 --> 00:14:18.950
See you again, Sakurato.

00:14:50.360 --> 00:14:51.870
We got one!

00:14:52.760 --> 00:14:53.870
Next!

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:56.680
<i>I can see.</i>

00:15:07.010 --> 00:15:09.070
Hey, Hizamaru-san!

00:15:10.490 --> 00:15:13.050
You're totally scared of the launch date.

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:16.310
You idiot. Of course I'm not.

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:17.960
I'm totally prepared!

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:20.600
Of course you are. But...

00:15:21.110 --> 00:15:22.930
Aren't you forgetting 
something really important?

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:24.390
Eh?

00:15:29.350 --> 00:15:30.950
Did you...

00:15:31.880 --> 00:15:34.270
I'm pretty good at stuff like this.

00:15:34.270 --> 00:15:35.500
Is it from your girlfriend?

00:15:35.830 --> 00:15:38.020
Well, maybe something like that...

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:41.270
I knew it. She's not coming to see you off?

00:15:43.440 --> 00:15:46.200
No, she's in Japan, awaiting my return.

00:15:46.830 --> 00:15:48.010
I see.

00:15:49.610 --> 00:15:50.890
I'm jealous,

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:53.500
since I might not be able to wait 
for your return, Hizamaru-san.

00:15:54.510 --> 00:15:58.390
Hopefully someone will be able to fix 
me up from my illness like that doll.

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:00.560
But it doesn't seem possible.

00:16:02.610 --> 00:16:05.100
<i>I heard you got acquainted 
with one of the patients.</i>

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:10.810
<i>This may sound harsh, but don't say anything</i>

00:16:10.810 --> 00:16:13.340
<i>that'll give them too much hope.</i>

00:16:17.680 --> 00:16:20.170
You'll get better! 
You'll definitely get better!

00:16:20.170 --> 00:16:21.070
Huh?

00:16:21.070 --> 00:16:23.560
We're going to Mars for research.

00:16:23.560 --> 00:16:25.570
We'll find the way to treat your illness

00:16:25.570 --> 00:16:27.880
from the organisms that only live there.

00:16:29.260 --> 00:16:30.230
Really?

00:16:31.430 --> 00:16:34.580
Sakurato! Is there something you 
want to do when you get better?

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:39.090
French... French fries! I want to eat fries!

00:16:39.090 --> 00:16:42.860
Sure. I'll buy you the large. What else?

00:16:44.090 --> 00:16:46.770
Teach me karate! I want to be macho, too!

00:16:46.770 --> 00:16:49.570
Sure thing. I'll even teach 
you some special moves.

00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:51.680
Oh, let's go to the ocean.

00:16:51.680 --> 00:16:52.560
Sure.

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:55.060
I want to see a major league game, too.

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:56.270
And eat pizza... and...

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:59.580
And then... And then...

00:16:57.750 --> 00:17:01.040
Even if we are safely able to return 
with a sample of the virus,

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:03.890
there's no guarantee 
we'll make it in time.

00:17:02.580 --> 00:17:03.890
Oh, I want to see a soccer match!

00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:11.170
Oh! I know! When I go back to 
Japan, I want to eat sushi.

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:23.620
It's all right to have hope for now.

00:17:24.160 --> 00:17:26.580
It's a hope that's small and far away,

00:17:27.210 --> 00:17:30.270
and now we can actually do something with it.

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:36.880
I want you to hold onto this doll...

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:39.400
and wait for my return!

00:17:49.950 --> 00:17:53.710
I will sever the root of 
this sadness no matter what!

00:17:54.560 --> 00:17:55.880
Leave it to me!

00:18:02.950 --> 00:18:05.270
Second one captured! Next!

00:18:06.340 --> 00:18:09.560
<i>I can't see unless I squint, but that's...</i>

00:18:26.100 --> 00:18:29.570
<i>String. But Akari's base isn't a spider...</i>

00:18:29.570 --> 00:18:31.490
<i>His medicine was in a syringe,</i>

00:18:32.410 --> 00:18:35.220
<i>meaning the surgery base was insect.</i>

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:38.790
<i>Not to mention those antennae...</i>

00:18:39.470 --> 00:18:40.720
<i>Is it a moth?</i>

00:18:54.660 --> 00:18:57.530
Three terraformar samples captured!

00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:24.810
I hear that my subordinate has 
captured about three of them.

00:19:26.610 --> 00:19:29.530
Because the species of the bug was rare,

00:19:29.530 --> 00:19:32.510
the surgery couldn't be 
done twenty years ago.

00:19:33.410 --> 00:19:36.110
But because we knew that his success rate

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:39.410
would be as high as Michelle 
K. Davis's, we were able to perform

00:19:39.410 --> 00:19:41.700
the surgery on Hizamaru Akari.

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:46.800
He is a powerful weapon for us...

00:19:47.400 --> 00:19:48.880
On Mars,

00:19:50.990 --> 00:19:52.970
and from now on.

00:20:04.730 --> 00:20:06.510
And there's the first batch.

00:20:06.900 --> 00:20:08.850
Waiting for the next one!

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:16.820
I'm glad my turn didn't come around.

00:20:18.300 --> 00:20:19.730
Damn...

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:22.890
Looks like it worked out somehow.

00:20:22.890 --> 00:20:26.350
Yeah. We already investigated 
the water here, right?

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:27.410
Yes.

00:20:27.700 --> 00:20:29.770
It's basically the same 
as the water on Earth.

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:34.790
Apparently this lake is rather deep 
just from the frozen soil melting.

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:35.970
Yeah.

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:38.550
Go ahead and call the others.

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:39.470
Got it.

00:20:40.030 --> 00:20:43.630
Damn it, that disgusting 
crap got into my collar.

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:49.800
The hell are you looking at, pervert?

00:20:51.300 --> 00:20:52.890
I'll go call everyone.

00:21:07.550 --> 00:21:08.740
Alex!

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:22.300
Michelle-san!

00:21:27.390 --> 00:21:28.140
Michelle-san!

00:21:28.140 --> 00:21:30.850
You idiot! Your job is over there!

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:40.700
Michelle-san!

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:43.070
Damn it!

00:21:44.230 --> 00:21:44.950
Everyone...

00:21:45.400 --> 00:21:46.930
Alex!

00:21:54.150 --> 00:21:56.540
<i>Well done, Akari.</i>

00:21:57.290 --> 00:21:59.250
<i>You're a good subordinate.</i>

00:22:03.770 --> 00:22:05.010
<i>I'm counting on you.</i>
